config SUNXI_G2D_FILLRECT_TEST
	tristate "Allwinner G2D RCQ fillrect self-test driver"
	depends on (ARM || ARM64) && HAS_IOMEM
	select DMA_COHERENT_POOL
	help
	  Build a minimal platform driver that brings up the Allwinner G2D
	  engine in RCQ mode and submits a single fill-rectangle command during
	  probe. The driver logs every stage (clock/reset enable, RCQ header
	  programming, STATUS polling) so that the hardware behaviour can be
	  diagnosed without touching the production BSP.

	  The driver is intended only for bring-up and hardware validation on
	  SoCs such as the T113-S3. It allocates its own test surface, performs
	  a 64x64 ARGB fill via RCQ and reports the observed status bits. No
	  user-space ABI is exposed.

	  Say Y here if you want to exercise the RCQ engine directly from the
	  kernel log for debugging purposes. The module can also be built
	  externally with M=m.
